A||||4||RZURCTN||Engine replacement in 84SE||||5
Z||000000||RZURCTN||10-05-1999||01:19 PM||||I am seriously considering replacing the engine in my 84SE.  As far as I know I can use any GM 2.5L type R engine of approx. the same year.  Does anyone know of anything special I should be looking for while searching for a replacement?  The only engines I can find locally are out of different makes and models.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-05-1999||04:29 PM||||All the 2.5's built on that block thru 1986 are directly compatible in your 84. Ideally you want to have an 86 with the roller lifter cam set. This motor makes a bit more power than previous versions. The roller lifter set reduces cam loads considerably wich also helps extend cam gear life.<P>While you have it out tho, I'd just go ahead and replace the cam gear set. No sence puting it in then having to rip things apart to change the gear a few months later.<P>You can use the motor from any other GM car BUT you will likely have to change some brackets and/or pulleys if you take one from a FWD car.<P>You cannot use a DIS motor in the cars built before 87 without replacing a whole lot of other things, inlcuding the ECM.<P>For safety make sure the new motor uses the same TBI. There may be a few 86 motors with the 700 TBI. The 700 is visibly diferant and is not plug compatible with the 300 TBI. If the new motor's TBI look like it cam from mars compaired to yours then it's the 700 and you don't want it. (The 700 TBI unit was not used in Fiero untill 87, but that doesn't mean GM didn't experiment in some other 86 modles)<P>Ideally you want to see and hear the motor run before you buy it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RZURCTN||10-05-1999||05:09 PM||||I looked a few engines and everything was pretty much the same with the exception of the brackets and distributor.  How can I tell the difference between one with roller lifters vs. one without? and would the timing gear be interchangeable?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan||10-05-1999||05:37 PM|||| bMy motor is out of an 85 olds Cierra. Not much to change around, and its real obvious.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-05-1999||08:25 PM||||the roller cam was only available begining in 86. I don't know if there is any external way to make sure you got one. look up the GM specs for that year car/motor combination.||||reg||1
